  "summary": "Entertainment space characterized by walls and ceilings covered with mirrors creating disorienting optical illusions.",
  "description": "Features environments with mirrored surfaces arranged at various angles to create infinite reflections, disorienting perspectives, and visual confusion, often combined with other elements like black lights, colored lighting, and obstacle courses. The aesthetic originated in European pleasure gardens and became a staple of carnivals, amusement parks, and funfairs, playing with perception and creating memorable disorienting experiences.",
